                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="10">
                                <p class="s38" style="font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;">
                                    The Federal Employees Retirement System, or FERS, became effective January 1, 1987.
                                    Almost all new employees hired after December 31, 1983, are automatically covered by
                                    FERS. Certain other Federal employees not covered by FERS have the option to
                                    transfer into the plan. The FERS Retirement System is composed of three tiers:
                                </p>
