                                    •
                                    <span style="padding-left: 5pt;color:black;">
                                        FERS-FRAE – Hired on/after 1/1/2014 – Code KF – Contribution 4.4%
                                    </span>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 2pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                    <span style="padding-left: 5pt;color:black;">
                                        Special Groups contributions are always .5% higher
                                    </span>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;">
                                    <b>Refunds</b> - You may withdrawyour basic benefit contributions if you leave
                                    Federal employment. However, if you do, you will not be eligible to receive benefits
                                    based on the service covered by the refund. There is no provision in the
                                    lawfortheredeposit of FERS contributionsthathavebeenrefunded.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;">
                                    <b>Retirement Options</b> - There are three categories of retirement benefits in the
                                    Basic Benefit Plan:
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;">
                                    <b>Immediate or Postponed</b> - If you meet one of the following sets of age and
                                    service requirements, you are entitled to an immediate retirement benefit:
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 2pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                    <span style="padding-left: 5pt;color:black;">
                                        Age 62 with at least 5 years of creditable service (unreduced benefit)
                                    </span>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 2pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                    <span style="padding-left: 5pt;color:black;">
                                        Age 60 with at least 20 years of creditable service (unreduced benefit)
                                    </span>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 2pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                    <span style="padding-left: 5pt;color:black;">
                                        MRA 30 (Minimum Retirement Age) with at least 30 years of service (see <a
                                            href="#chart" style="color: blue;">chart</a> on Page 11)
                                    </span>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 2pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                    <span style="padding-left: 5pt;color:black;">
                                        MRA 10 (Minimum Retirement Age) with at least 10 years of service
                                    </span>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 5pt;font-size: 10pt;text-align: center;color: red;">
                                    <i>Note: MRA 10 – If you retire under MRA 10 (at least 10 years of service but less
                                        than 30 years), your FERS annuity will be reduced by 5% for every year you are
                                        under the age of 62.</i>
                                </p>
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 8pt;padding-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: center;">
                                    <b>Unless you have 20 years of service and your annuity begins at age 60 or later,
                                        you can avoid part, or all of the reduction by postponing the commencing date of
                                        your annuity.</b>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;">
                                    <b>Early Retirement</b> - An early retirement benefit is available in certain
                                    involuntary separation cases and in cases of voluntary separations, during a major
                                    reorganization, or reduction in force. To be eligible, you must meet the following
                                    requirements:
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 2pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                    <span style="padding-left: 5pt;color:black;">
                                        Age 50 with 20 years of service
                                    </span>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 2pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                    <span style="padding-left: 5pt;color:black;">
                                        Any age with 25 years of service
                                    </span>
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;color: #2E5395;">
                                    •
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
                                <p class="s38"
                                    style="padding-top: 5pt;padding-left: 5pt;margin-left: 5pt;font-size: 11pt;text-align: justify;">
                                    <b>Deferred Retirement</b> - If you leave Federal service before you meet the age
                                    and service requirements for an immediate retirement benefit, you may be eligible
                                    for deferred retirement benefits. To be eligible, you must have completed at least 5
                                    years of creditable civilian service. You may receive benefits when you meet one of
                                    the following sets of age and service requirements:
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="1">
                                <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
                                </p>
                            </td>
                            <td colspan="9">
